From abda21217f58777d92db0e777550caa22c373b80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Test the engines floor instead of asserting it

`package.json` declares `engines.node: ">=22"`, and the matrix ran 24.x
and latest, so the floor was never exercised. A floor CI does not run is
a claim, and this package's posture is that a claim nothing checks goes
stale: ">=24" stood unexamined until someone noticed the entire Node
surface is three node:crypto imports present since Node 16, against a
target of es2021.

Adding 22.x makes the lowest supported version the one the suite proves.
It costs three more matrix cells.

Remove patch/engines-floor-matrix.patch and its row in patch/README.md
in the commit that applies this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W4X2MprZjtGPiBVth8jTrW
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index 93b7a47..46c7474 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ jobs:
       fail-fast: false
       matrix:
         os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest]
-        node-version: [24.x, latest]
+        node-version: [22.x, 24.x, latest]
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
-- 
